it was a brutal murky murder in a pub  car park but was daniel morgan killed to  stop him exposing police corruption  today's report finds that police  corruption not only  hampered the investigation into his  murder it frustrated efforts to get to  the truth  for decades and that corruption remains  within the metropolitan police  34 years later concealing or denying  failings for the sake of an  organization's public image  is dishonesty on the part of the  organization  for reputational benefit this  constitutes  a form of institutional corruption  while the report discovered multiple  mistakes and misconduct such as  investigating officers drinking with  known suspects  it couldn't say whether corrupt police  were involved in the murder  but warned it was possible that local  officers involved in identified  lucrative corrupt practices such as  assisting criminals with inside police  information  thought that their police careers and  pensions were under threat  and the evidence supporting this theory  as to why daniel morgan was murdered  was never seriously investigated is the  metropolitan police force  institutionally corrupt  that's a phrase which of course has been  coined by this report so we need to  carefully consider the evidence upon  which that assertion is based but  my initial response of course is no  i believe in this organization the  report authors say the forces first  objective was to protect itself  even the panel struggled to get access  to police documents  and the family is owed an apology we  found ourselves lied to  fobbed off bullied degraded  and let down time and time again  what we were required to endure was  nothing less than torture  the metropolitan police commissioner who  today apologized  is under fire from daniel morgan's  family uh yes i do think she should be  considering that position  should she go uh yes certainly  it's a damning report it reveals sadly  significant corruption  but the woman who commissioned the  report as home secretary  defended cressida dick i've worked with  cressida dick both as home secretary  and as prime minister she is an  extraordinarily able police officer  the home secretary has asked her to  respond to this report  and i'm sure that's exactly what she  will want to do  the gruesome attack in an isolated car  park has resulted  in five investigations costing an  estimated  30 million pounds multiple arrests  but not a single conviction so let's  look at the timeline  in march 1987 the body of private  investigator daniel morgan is found with  an axe embedded in his head at the  golden lion pub in sydney  he's killed shortly after meeting his  business partner jonathan reese for a  drink  a month later six people are arrested on  suspicion of murder  they include mr reese and sid fillery a  metropolitan police detective originally  assigned  to the case all are released without  charge and there are four more  investigations over the years involving  the bugging of suspects homes  as well as the offices of mr reese in  2008  four men are charged with daniel  morgan's murder  including jonathan reece but three years  later at the old bailey the case against  the men collapsed jonathan reese and sid  fillery  who've throughout maintained their  innocence go on to win damages for  malicious prosecution  the metropolitan police made a litany of  mistakes  and that this irreparably damaged the  chances of successful prosecution  this is one of the most devastating  episodes in the history of the  metropolitan police  some suggestions in this 1200 page  report  point to reopening the case but it does  say crucial evidence has almost  certainly been lost jason farrell sky  news
 

